name: sim.writeCustomStringData
description: Deprecated. See properties instead
luaSynopsis: sim.writeCustomStringData(int objectHandle, string tagName, string/bytes data)
pythonSynopsis: sim.writeCustomStringData(int objectHandle, string tagName, string data)
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object where you want to store your data, sim.handle_scene, sim.handle_app or sim.handle_appstorage
2. tagName: string that identifies the data. An empty string removes all custom data
3. data: your custom data. If empty, the current data under the specified dataName is removed
outputs:
replacedBy:
- name: setStringProperty, class: object, object_setStringProperty.method, note: "use a 'customData.'-prefix for the property name"
